# What NOT to upload as build input.
#
# Vercel serves only `dist/` (outputDirectory in vercel.json), so nothing listed
# here was ever reachable by a visitor. This keeps the upload to what
# `node build.mjs` actually reads.

# Built here by the build command, so shipping a local copy only risks a stale one.
dist/
node_modules/

# Editor and agent state.
.claude/
.vscode/

# Docs — read by people, not by the build.
README.md

# supabase.sql is NOT ignored. It used to be, because only people read it. The
# build command now runs tools/check.mjs, which reads it to prove every form
# field still has a column — so it is a build input, and ignoring it here makes
# the deploy fail on a missing file rather than pass.

# Host configs for Cloudflare Pages, Netlify and Apache. Kept in the repo so the
# site can move hosts without a rewrite; Vercel reads vercel.json instead and
# these would only confuse the picture.
_headers
_redirects
.htaccess
